messages.content:
{
  "message": "I can help you with your MMS (picture messaging) issue. First, I need to verify your account for technical support. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for providing your information, John. To help resolve your MMS issue, I’ll need to run a few checks on your phone. Could you please confirm if you are able to send and receive regular text messages (SMS) and if your mobile data is working for browsing the web or using apps? This will help me determine where the problem might be."
}

{
  "message": "No problem, I can guide you through checking your mobile data. On your phone, please look at the top of your screen (the status bar) and let me know if you see any of these icons: 5G, 4G, LTE, 3G, H+, or E. Also, let me know if you see any icons that look like an airplane or say 'No Signal.' This will help me understand your current connection. If you’re not sure, I can walk you through a quick check—just let me know!"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you, that’s very helpful! Since you have a 5G connection and mobile data appears to be on, your phone should be able to send MMS. The next step is to check if your messaging app has the necessary permissions to send picture messages. Please follow these steps:

1. Grant SMS permission to your messaging app. On your phone, go to Settings > Apps > Messaging > Permissions, and make sure SMS is allowed.

Let me know once you’ve done this, and I’ll guide you to the next step."
}

{
  "message": "Yes, please go ahead and allow storage permission for your messaging app. This is necessary for sending and receiving picture messages (MMS). Once you have allowed storage permission, let me know so we can check if your MMS is working or continue troubleshooting if needed."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for updating the permissions. I have also added 2GB of extra data to your line to ensure you have enough data for sending picture messages. Please try sending an MMS now. If it still doesn't work, let me know and we can continue troubleshooting."
}

{
  "message": "I'm glad to hear that your picture messages are working now! To keep things running smoothly, just make sure your messaging app always has SMS and storage permissions, and that your mobile data is turned on when you want to send or receive MMS. If you ever run low on data or have similar issues again, feel free to reach out for help. Have a great day!"
}

{
  "message": "I can help you troubleshoot your mobile data issues. First, I need to identify your account to check your line and plan details. Could you please provide your phone number, customer ID, or your full name and date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you, John. To begin troubleshooting your mobile data issues, please turn Airplane Mode ON and then OFF on your phone. This can help reset your network connection. Let me know once you have done this, and we’ll continue with the next steps."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for completing that step. Next, please set your phone’s network mode preference to '4G/5G Preferred.' This will help your device connect to the fastest available network and can improve your internet speed. Let me know once you’ve done this so we can continue troubleshooting if needed."
}

{
  "message": "Great job! Now, let's check your current internet speed to ensure it's excellent. Please run a speed test on your phone and let me know the result. This will help us determine if your connection meets your expectations or if further troubleshooting is needed."
}

{
  "message": "Your internet speed is excellent at 275 Mbps, which is well above typical requirements for most activities. Your connection is now set up for optimal performance. If you experience any further issues or notice a drop in speed, feel free to reach out for more help. Otherwise, you’re all set!"
}

{
  "message": "I can help you with your MMS issue. First, I need to verify your account for technical support. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for verifying your information, John. To help resolve your MMS issue, I’ll need to guide you through a few quick checks and actions on your phone. First, could you please check if you are able to make regular calls and use mobile data (for example, browsing the web)? This will help determine if the issue is specific to MMS or related to your overall service."
}

{
  "message": "Yes, please turn off Airplane Mode on your phone. Once it is off, try making a call or using mobile data to browse the web. Let me know if you are able to do so, and if you are still having trouble sending MMS messages after turning off Airplane Mode."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for the update. The next step is to make sure your phone is set to use the best available network mode for MMS. Please set your network mode preference to '4G/5G preferred' on your phone. Let me know once you have done this, and if you are still unable to send MMS messages."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for your patience. The next step is to check your phone's APN settings, as incorrect APN or missing MMSC information can prevent MMS from working. Please check your APN settings and let me know if the MMSC URL is set. If you’re unsure how to check, I can guide you through the process."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for confirming your MMSC URL. The next step is to check if Wi-Fi Calling is enabled, as it can sometimes interfere with MMS. Please check if Wi-Fi Calling is currently ON. If it is, please turn it OFF and then try sending an MMS again. Let me know if this resolves the issue or if you need further assistance."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for checking that. The next step is to ensure your messaging app has the necessary permissions to send and receive MMS. Please check if your messaging app has both 'storage' and 'SMS' permissions enabled. If either is missing, please enable them. Let me know if you need instructions on how to check or change these permissions, or if the permissions are already set correctly."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for confirming the app permissions. Since we've checked Airplane Mode, network mode, APN settings, Wi-Fi Calling, and app permissions, the next step is to try resetting your APN settings to default. After resetting, you will need to reboot your device for the changes to take effect. Please reset your APN settings now, and let me know once you have done so. I will then guide you to reboot your device."
}

{
  "message": "Great! The next step is to reboot your device to apply the new APN settings. Please restart your phone now. Once your phone has restarted, try sending an MMS message again and let me know if the issue is resolved."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for following all the steps so far. Since we've tried all standard troubleshooting steps for MMS issues—including checking service, data, network mode, APN settings, Wi-Fi Calling, and app permissions—and the problem persists, I will need to escalate your case to a human technical support agent for further assistance. Please hold on while I transfer you."
}

{
  "message": "YOU ARE BEING TRANSFERRED TO A HUMAN AGENT. PLEASE HOLD ON."
}
